fix(panic): keep the USB console or reboot after a panic

A panic that stops the console's transmit gate used to park forever:
ud_panic_takeover() only took over when ml_dbgwrap_cpu_is_halted()
reported the recorded owner stopped.  That API reads the DBGWRAP DBGACK
bit of the Apple CoreSight UTT window, which this board's generated ADT
does not map, and a SIGPdebug-parked CPU never sets it either.  The
panic loop then retried the refused takeover every millisecond without
ever polling the controller: the CDC-ACM port stayed enumerated while
every bulk write timed out, and this board has no watchdog reset.

Take over unconditionally once panic_active(): fence the controller
with ud_controller_restart(), then clear the transmit gate, the receive
lock and the log producer.  If the console still cannot be serviced
(takeover refused for a second, controller reset failed, or the console
never came up), print one diagnostic line and reset through
PEHaltRestart(kPERestartCPU) instead of parking.

Make the default panic policy safe as well: KEBAB now clears
panicDebugging unless a debugger was explicitly requested through
kebabkdp=1 or kdp_match_name.  debug=0x14e alone no longer parks in
"Waiting for remote debugger connection"; DB_HALT and kebabkdp=1 keep
their existing debugger behaviour.  Panic restart types that cannot
enter the console pump now reach PSCI SYSTEM_RESET instead of returning
-1 and letting halt_all_cpus() park the board.

The panic report, EP0 probe dump, port reopen, KDP attach, REBOOT and
FASTBOOT paths are unchanged.

